-- title:
--   Regularity of the 1/j-chart at cusps off the floor cusp ∞
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero, and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\zeta=e^{2\pi i/q}$ and that $L$ is algebraic over $\mathbb Q$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((t))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H$ at level $q^2M'$, where $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K$, $j\ne 0$, have image in $L((t))$ the coefficientwise image of the expansion $\mathrm{jq}=t^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series part of }j)$, and let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f\in W_0$ exactly when there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((t))$ after applying $A\to L$. Write $B=\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j$ for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. The assertion is: for every prime ideal $y$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$, containing the element $j^{-1}$ of $B$, containing every $b\in B$ whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$, and such that it is *not* the case that for all $b\in B$ whose expansion lies in the field obtained from $L$ by adjoining the expansions $j(q^d)$ for $d\mid q^2M'$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if the $0$-th coefficient of $b$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$, and for every commutative ring $B_m$ that is a $B$-algebra realising the localisation of $B$ at $y$: $B_m$ is a regular local ring and so is $B_m$ modulo the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the cusp-regularity statement for the integral two-chart model of $X_H(q^2M')$ over $A$ at a closed point on the $j^{-1}$-chart lying over a cusp of the $\Gamma_0$-quotient different from $\infty$, asserting both regularity of the local ring and regularity of its fibre over the closed point of $A$. It feeds the companion statement handling the points over the cusp $\infty$, from which the regularity of the model along the whole cuspidal fibre is assembled.
-- source:
